 [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_016: mol_017 -> mol_006 (Aminoacetaldehyde Oxidation to Glycine) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_017: mol_018 -> mol_006 (N-oxalylglycine Hydrolysis to Glycine) [Surface]\n  - rxn_018: mol_008, mol_002 -> mol_018 (Glyoxylate + Ammonia Condensation to N-oxalylglycine) [Surface]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Surface Strecker (Classical Miller\u2013Urey) (3 steps)\n  - P2: Cyanosulfidic\u2013Glycolonitrile Branch (4 steps)\n  - P3: Non-Cyanide Glyoxylate Aza-Cannizzaro Reaction (1 steps)\n  - P4: Alkaline Hydrothermal FeS\u2013Fe\u2070 Reductive Amination (1 steps)\n  - P5: Nitrate\u2013Ferroan Brucite System (1 steps)\n  - P6: Bucherer\u2013Bergs Hydantoin Pathway (2 steps)\n  - P7: Formaldehyde\u2013Hydroxylamine Route to Aminoacetonitrile (4 steps)\n  - P8: Formaldehyde\u2013Ammonia Polymer Route (1 steps)\n  - P9: Impact Shock (Formic Acid + Ammonium Nitrate) (1 steps)\n  - P10: Ethanolamine Oxidation Route (2 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK (RDKit) ===\nComputed programmatically from each molecule's InChI (via RDKit) or stated formula. Reactions list no coefficients, so a reaction counts as balanced if some positive integer coefficients (<= 24) conserve every element and net charge.\nSummary: 18 reactions | 1 balanced as written | 0 balanceable with coefficients | 15 UNBALANCED | 2 unchecked\n  - rxn_001 UNBALANCED: CH2O + NH3 + HCN -> NH2CH2CN | reactants minus products: H+2, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product; CO2 as product; O2 as product\n  - rxn_002 UNBALANCED: NH2CH2CN -> NH2CH2CONH2 | reactants minus products: H-2, O-1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as reactant\n  - rxn_003 UNBALANCED: NH2CH2CONH2 -> NH2CH2COOH | reactants minus products: H+1, N+1, O-1 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_005 UNBALANCED: HOCH2CN + NH3 -> NH2CH2CN | reactants minus products: H+2, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product\n  - rxn_006 UNBALANCED: OHC(COOH) + NH3 -> NH2CH2COOH | reactants min