in (glycolonitrile).\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Documented in prebiotic cyanide/aldehyde solutions (Patel et al., 2015; Miller, 1957; classical Strecker branch).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_006\",\n      \"name\": \"Amination of glycolonitrile to aminoacetonitrile\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_002\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_004\", \"mol_023\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-350K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": null\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Nucleophilic displacement of hydroxyl by ammonia leads to aminoacetonitrile; formaldehyde as byproduct.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Well-established for \u03b1-cyanohydrin ammonia displacement (Patel et al., 2015).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_007\",\n      \"name\": \"Glyoxylate formation from formaldehyde and water via oxidation\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_001\", \"mol_022\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_008\", \"mol_024\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [\"UV radiation\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"280-320K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"Clay minerals, UV\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"Surface photochemistry\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Photo-oxidation of formaldehyde produces glyoxylate and releases protons.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Photo-oxidative mechanisms observed on mineral/UV-exposed surfaces for C1 to C2 carbonyl conversion (Patel et al., 2015; Li et al., 2024).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_008\",\n      \"name\": \"Aza-Cannizzaro glycine formation from glyoxylate and ammonium\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_008\", \"mol_017\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_007\", \"mol_025\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": 