 \"Formamide decomposition/radicalization and coupling on mineral surface; produces glycine, N-formylglycine, CO2.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Saladino et al., 2015. Yields and conditions resemble irradiation/meteoritic flux.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pathways\": [\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P1\",\n      \"name\": \"Classical Strecker Synthesis\",\n      \"description\": \"Discharge-generated formaldehyde, HCN, and ammonia undergoe Strecker synthesis to produce aminoacetonitrile, hydrolyzed to glycinamide and then glycine.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_002\", \"rxn_003\", \"rxn_004\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_004\", \"mol_006\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P2\",\n      \"name\": \"Glycolonitrile\u2013Amination Branch\",\n      \"description\": \"Formaldehyde and HCN react to form glycolonitrile, which is aminated to aminoacetonitrile, then hydrolyzed to glycinamide and glycine.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_005\", \"rxn_006\", \"rxn_003\", \"rxn_004\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_004\", \"mol_006\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P3\",\n      \"name\": \"Aza-Cannizzaro Disproportionation\",\n      \"description\": \"Formaldehyde is oxidized to glyoxylate, which reacts with ammonium via the aza-Cannizzaro mechanism to give glycine and oxamate.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_007\", \"rxn_008\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_008\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P4\",\n      \"name\": \"FeS/Fe0 Reductive Amination\",\n      \"description\": \"Surface- or hydrothermally-produced glyoxylate is reductively aminated with ammonia on FeS/Fe0 minerals to yield glycine.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_007\", \"rxn_009\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_008\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P5\",\n      \"name\": \"Nitrate\u2013Brucite Integration\",\n      \"description\": \"Nitrate is reduced by Fe(II) in brucite mineral to ammo